  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="35.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 35.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-g2">Sit nomen Domini benedictum et rel.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-d">Sit nomen Domini benedictum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-d">Sit nomen Domini benedictum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Blessed be the name of the Lord.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Der Name des Herrn sei gepriesen u. s. w. G2 D)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Blessed be the name of the Lord, etc. G2 D)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Not in G (so K is empty). In G2 the so-called ‘Polity’ (Thorpe p. 422) follows; in D, three Old English chapters on the Decalogue and the cardinal vices and virtues, then I As.</note>
      </div>
